# @rt-category Test Scenes
# @rt-description A thin uniform NanoVDB cube lit by a distant light, seen on a black background: the single-scattered radiance has a closed form.
# @rt-performance Fast
# nanovdb-thin-slab.pbrt -- the absolute check of the NanoVDB medium's density, size and placement.
#
# A white furnace cannot see the density: a medium that only scatters is invisible under a uniform sky whatever its density, so the furnace passes
# even with a wrong majorant. This scene measures the density instead. pbrt_scenes/nanovdb-fire-test.nvdb is a 4x4x4-voxel grid (native box [0,4]^3) of
# uniform density 0.5. Scaled by 0.05 and centred, it is a cube 0.2 units on a side. With sigma_s = 0.1 the optical depth through it is about 0.01,
# so scattering is almost all single, and the radiance a camera ray through the middle of the cube sees is
#
#     L = sigma_s * (integral of density along the ray) * E / (4 pi)       (isotropic phase, g = 0; E = 1 for a distant light of L = 1)
#
# The integral is not 0.5 * 0.2. pbrt reads a sampled grid at the voxel CENTRES and treats everything outside the grid as zero (SampledGrid::Lookup,
# src/pbrt/util/containers.h: p * n - 0.5, out-of-range lookups give 0), so the density falls linearly from 0.5 at the centre of the outermost voxel to
# 0.25 at the box face. Along the ray through the middle: the inner three quarters of the 0.2 are at 0.5, and each outer eighth averages 0.375, giving
# 0.2 * (0.75 * 0.5 + 0.25 * 0.375) = 0.09375 (6.25% less than the naive 0.1). So
#
#     L = 0.1 * 0.09375 / (4 pi) = 7.46e-4
#
# The camera sees only the middle of the cube (fov 0.5 degrees from 5 units away), so that holds for every pixel. Doubling the density, the size or the
# scattering scale doubles the answer; dropping the half-voxel fade adds 6.7%. The single-scatter formula ignores attenuation (about -1%) and multiple
# scattering (about +0.5%); the test allows 3% for those and for sampling noise.
#
# Original, so it carries no licence constraints beyond NanoVDB's own for the bundled .nvdb file (src/external/nanovdb/LICENSE).

LookAt  0 0 5    0 0 0    0 1 0
Camera "perspective" "float fov" [ 0.5 ]

Film "rgb" "integer xresolution" [ 64 ] "integer yresolution" [ 64 ]
Sampler "halton" "integer pixelsamples" [ 64 ]

WorldBegin

LightSource "distant" "point3 from" [ 0 1 0 ] "point3 to" [ 0 0 0 ] "rgb L" [ 1 1 1 ]

# CTM = Translate * Scale: a native point p lands at 0.05 p - 0.1, so the grid's [0,4]^3 becomes [-0.1, 0.1]^3.
AttributeBegin
  Translate -0.1 -0.1 -0.1
  Scale 0.05 0.05 0.05
  MakeNamedMedium "slab" "string type" [ "nanovdb" ]
    "string filename" [ "nanovdb-fire-test.nvdb" ]
    "rgb sigma_a" [ 0 0 0 ] "rgb sigma_s" [ 0.1 0.1 0.1 ] "float g" [ 0 ]
AttributeEnd

# The trigger sphere: radius 0.2 is past the cube's half-diagonal (0.173).
AttributeBegin
  Material "interface"
  MediumInterface "slab" ""
  Shape "sphere" "float radius" [ 0.2 ]
AttributeEnd
